  "pre_stated_hypothesis": "IQR_t = rolling Interquartile Range of qvol[t-W+1..t], W=48: Q1_t=percentile(qvol_{t-W+1..t},25), Q3_t=percentile(qvol_{t-W+1..t},75), IQR_t=Q3_t-Q1_t (robust rank/order-statistic dispersion of middle 50%). i_z=zscore(IQR_t,ZLB=168). Mean-revert rank-dispersion shocks: i_z>=1.25 SHORT (abnormally wide IQR/expanded middle dispersion; fade), i_z<=-1.25 LONG (abnormally narrow IQR/compressed middle dispersion; fade), exit |i_z|<0.25 or hold>=12 or flip. Exec t->t+1. WF 720/168/168. Cost grid 0-40bps. Edge iff exposure>0 AND all slices OOS net>0 AND >B&H. Genuinely different from C23/C40-C61.",
  "hypothesis_differs_from_c23_c40_c61": "C62=rolling IQR (Q3-Q1), rank/order-statistic dispersion of the middle 50% using two quartile cutpoints; ignores tails beyond Q1/Q3. C61=rolling MAD median(|x-median(x)|), L1 robust scale using absolute deviations of ALL in-window observations centered at median \u2014 different estimator, different robustness profile/quantity. C48=rolling STD (L2, mean-based 2nd-moment, outlier-sensitive). C56=CV=std/mean (relative L2 ratio). C49=kurtosis; C50=skewness (standardized higher moments). C57=Shannon value-bin entropy; C58=Bandt\u2013Pompe permutation entropy; C60=Sample Entropy template regularity (none are dispersion magnitude). C59=Hurst R/S fractal scaling exponent. C51=lag-1 autocorr. C52/C53/C55=cross-corrs; C54=OLS beta. C45=Amihud. C46=OBV signed-cumulative. C47=up/down imbalance. C43=unsloped divergence; C44=ROC. C23/40/41/42=vol_z level/expansion. None is a rolling interquartile range rank-quartile dispersion; C62 orthogonal to all transforms in C23/C40-C61.",
